    engineeringData: { blockDesign: "V8 (90-degree), Closed-deck Aluminum block with cast iron cylinder liners. The N63TU (Technical Update) is a massive improvement over the disastrous original N63. The block is phenomenally rigid. The 'Hot-V' configuration places the turbos in the valley between the cylinders, drastically reducing exhaust travel distance and practically eliminating turbo lag. However, this design traps unimaginable heat, destroying every plastic and rubber component nearby.", crankshaft: "Forged Steel, supported by 5 main bearings. Features a cross-plane design.", pistonSpeed: "15.4 m/s @ 6500 RPM.", alternator: "220A Valeo.", rotatingAssembly: { pistonConstruction: "Cast aluminum alloy. Features a 10.0:1 compression ratio. CRITICALLY: The N63TU introduced forged connecting rods, making the bottom end significantly stronger and more capable of handling tuning than the original N63.", wristPinDiameter: "22 mm.", connectingRodLength: "143 mm.", rodBoltSize: "M10.", crankMainJournal: "70.0 mm.", crankRodJournal: "48.0 mm.", rodRatio: "1.73." }, cylinderHead: { combustionChamberVol: "Pent-roof design with centrally located injectors.", intakePortFlow: "32-valve DOHC design. The intake manifolds are uniquely placed on the OUTSIDE of the cylinder banks, while the exhaust ports face the INSIDE 'V'. CRITICALLY: The N63TU added Valvetronic (variable valve lift) to the V8, drastically improving throttle response and efficiency.", valveSizes: "Intake: 33.0 mm / Exhaust: 29.0 mm.", valveStemDiameter: "6.0 mm.", camshaftDuration: "Highly variable via Double-VANOS and Valvetronic.", lifterType: "Hydraulic bucket tappets.", specialFeature: "US Spec Tune & The Solenoid Injector Fix. This US market variant is slightly detuned on paper to 445hp (from the EU 450hp) to meet ULEV emissions. The absolute most important update for the N63TU was ditching the catastrophically unreliable Piezo injectors of the original N63. The TU utilizes robust Bosch solenoid injectors, completely eliminating the terrifying risk of overnight fuel leaking and hydrolocking the engine." }, oilAndCooling: { oilSquirters: "Yes, under-piston cooling jets.", oilPumpType: "Chain-driven variable displacement map-controlled pump.", thermostatOpening: "Electronically mapped by the ECU (ranges from 90°C to 105°C).", oilCooler: "Massive integrated liquid-to-liquid heat exchanger." }, fuelSystem: { systemType: "Bosch High Precision Direct Injection.", maxPressure: "200 Bar (Fuel Rail). Uses two mechanical high-pressure fuel pumps.", injectors: "8x Bosch Solenoid Injectors (Vastly more reliable than early Piezo units)." }, tuningLimits: { maxSafeTorqueStock: "800 Nm (The heavy-duty ZF 8HP70 transmission handles this perfectly).", maxSafePowerStock: "600 hp (The forged rods in the N63TU block handle this safely, but high heat risks component failure).", maxSafeRPM: "6500 RPM", weakestLink: "Valve Stem Seals (Massive oil burning), Hot-V Cooling Lines (Fire risk), OFHG Oil Leak (Belt Ingestion), Ignition Coils." }, electrical: { coils: "Individual Coil Pack system (Bosch).", ecu: "Dual Bosch MEVD17.2.8 (Highly tunable via OBD)." } },
    recommendedParts: { description: "Crucial maintenance parts to prevent catastrophic engine failure, fires, and oil burning on the incredibly hot N63TU V8 engine.", parts: [ { category: "Hot-V Turbo Cooling Lines", brand: "Genuine BMW / Billet", note: "CRITICAL: Plastic 'T' fittings crack. Upgrade to billet aluminum." }, { category: "Valve Stem Seal Kit", brand: "Elring / Victor Reinz", note: "CRITICAL: Fixes massive blue smoke. Must use AGA Tools." }, { category: "Oil Filter Housing Gasket (OFHG)", brand: "Genuine BMW", note: "CRITICAL: Fixes oil leak that causes fatal belt ingestion." }, { category: "105Ah AGM Battery", brand: "Varta / Genuine BMW", note: "CRITICAL: The hot-V cooling fans kill batteries rapidly." }, { category: "Ignition Coils (x8)", brand: "Eldor / Bosch", note: "Replace proactively to maintain smooth twin-turbo delivery." }, { category: "Spark Plugs", brand: "NGK SILZKBR8D8S", note: "Requires 8 units. Replace strictly every 30k miles." }, { category: "High-Pressure Fuel Pump (x2)", brand: "Bosch", note: "Common failure causing long cranks and limp mode." }, { category: "Front Thrust Arms (Control Arms)", brand: "Lemförder", note: "Fixes severe F15 braking shimmy." } ] },
